{"name":"Lemon Curd","hex":"#ffee11","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lemon curd","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick preserve made from lemons (juice and zest), egg yolk, butter and sugar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemon_curd"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fruit curd","blocks":[{"text":"Fruit curd is a dessert sauce, prepared similarly to custard but with fruit juice instead of milk or cream. It is usually, though not always, made with citrus fruit. Curds are often used as fillings and spreads in cakes, pastries, tarts, and other desserts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Lemoncurd.jpg/330px-Lemoncurd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit_curd","wikidata":"Q1799855"},{"title":"Lemon","blocks":[{"text":"The lemon is a species of small evergreen tree in the Citrus genus of the flowering plant family Rutaceae. A true lemon is a hybrid of the citron and the bitter orange. Its origins are uncertain, but some evidence suggests lemons originated during the 1st millennium BC in what is now northeastern India. Some other citrus fruits are called lemon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/P1030323.JPG/330px-P1030323.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","wikidata":"Q500"},{"title":"Curd","blocks":[{"text":"Curd is obtained by coagulating milk in a sequential process called curdling. It can be a final dairy product or the first stage in cheesemaking. The coagulation can be caused by adding rennet, a culture, or any edible acidic substance such as lemon juice or vinegar, and then allowing it to coagulate. The increased acidity causes the milk proteins (casein) to tangle into solid masses, or curds. Milk that has been left to sour will also automatically produce curds, and sour milk cheeses are produced this way."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Curd_Setting.jpg/330px-Curd_Setting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curd","wikidata":"Q622563"},{"title":"Lemon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemon or lemon-color is a vivid yellow color characteristic of the lemon fruit. Shades of \"lemon\" may vary significantly from the fruit's actual color, including fluorescent tones and creamy hues reflective of lemon pies and confections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg/330px-Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2720565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Vegan_Lemon_Curd_%2848839115308%29.jpg/120px-Vegan_Lemon_Curd_%2848839115308%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Vegan_Lemon_Curd_%2848839115308%29.jpg/250px-Vegan_Lemon_Curd_%2848839115308%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Vegan_Lemon_Curd_%2848839115308%29.jpg/120px-Vegan_Lemon_Curd_%2848839115308%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVegan_Lemon_Curd_(48839115308).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Orange_curd.jpg/120px-Orange_curd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Orange_curd.jpg/250px-Orange_curd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Orange_